---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Breadcrumbs from '../components/Breadcrumbs.astro';
import Callout from '../components/Callout.astro';
---
<BaseLayout
  title="How Money Really Works — Indian Scams, Fraud & Laws — Artha Atlas"
  description="Forensic analysis of Indian financial crimes, unregistered deposit schemes under BUDS Act 2019, Ponzi mechanics, stock market manipulation, and real case studies."
>
  <div class="max-w-5xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 py-8 sm:py-12">
    <Breadcrumbs items={[{ label: 'How Money Really Works: Scams & Fraud' }]} />

    <header class="my-6 pb-6 border-b border-stone-200 dark:border-stone-800">
      <div class="inline-flex items-center space-x-2 text-xs font-mono font-semibold text-red-700 dark:text-red-400 bg-red-50 dark:bg-red-950/60 border border-red-200 dark:border-red-900 px-3 py-1 rounded-full mb-3">
        <span>🚨 Forensic Investor Protection</span>
        <span>•</span>
        <span>Criminal Statutes & Penalties</span>
      </div>
      <h1 class="text-3xl sm:text-5xl font-serif font-bold text-stone-900 dark:text-stone-50 tracking-tight leading-tight">
        How Money Really Works — Legally and Illegally
      </h1>
      <p class="text-base sm:text-lg text-stone-600 dark:text-stone-300 max-w-4xl mt-3 font-sans leading-relaxed">
        The financial system is riddled with traps designed to separate uneducated retail investors from their capital. Below is a forensic breakdown of how financial fraud operates in India, the governing statutes, and red flags.
      </p>
    </header>

    <div class="space-y-12">
      <!-- Statutory Framework -->
      <section class="space-y-4">
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-serif font-bold text-stone-900 dark:text-stone-100">
          The Governing Indian Anti-Fraud Statutes
        </h2>
        <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 gap-4 text-xs sm:text-sm">
          <div class="p-4 rounded-xl bg-white dark:bg-stone-900 border border-stone-200 dark:border-stone-800">
            <h3 class="font-serif font-bold text-base text-stone-900 dark:text-stone-100 mb-1">
              📜 BUDS Act, 2019
            </h3>
            <p class="text-stone-600 dark:text-stone-400 leading-relaxed">
              The <em>Banning of Unregulated Deposit Schemes Act, 2019</em> bans any deposit-taking activity not approved by a designated regulator (RBI, SEBI, IRDAI, PFRDA, MCA). It imposes 1 to 10 years of rigorous imprisonment and disgorgement of assets.
            </p>
          </div>

          <div class="p-4 rounded-xl bg-white dark:bg-stone-900 border border-stone-200 dark:border-stone-800">
            <h3 class="font-serif font-bold text-base text-stone-900 dark:text-stone-100 mb-1">
              📜 SEBI (PFUTP) Regulations, 2003
            </h3>
            <p class="text-stone-600 dark:text-stone-400 leading-relaxed">
              <em>Prohibition of Fraudulent and Unfair Trade Practices relating to Securities Market</em>. Outlaws pump-and-dump syndicates, circular trading, misleading research reports, and front-running by asset managers.
            </p>
          </div>

          <div class="p-4 rounded-xl bg-white dark:bg-stone-900 border border-stone-200 dark:border-stone-800">
            <h3 class="font-serif font-bold text-base text-stone-900 dark:text-stone-100 mb-1">
              📜 PMLA, 2002 (Money Laundering)
            </h3>
            <p class="text-stone-600 dark:text-stone-400 leading-relaxed">
              Enforced by the Enforcement Directorate (ED). Targets placement, layering, and integration of illicit capital through hawala networks, shell corporations, and crypto rails.
            </p>
          </div>

          <div class="p-4 rounded-xl bg-white dark:bg-stone-900 border border-stone-200 dark:border-stone-800">
            <h3 class="font-serif font-bold text-base text-stone-900 dark:text-stone-100 mb-1">
              📜 Benami Transactions Act, 1988 (Amended 2016)
            </h3>
            <p class="text-stone-600 dark:text-stone-400 leading-relaxed">
              Prohibits holding real estate, equity shares, or bank accounts under fictitious names or proxies. Confiscation of property without compensation and up to 7 years imprisonment.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <!-- Forensic Scam Categories -->
      <section class="space-y-6">
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-serif font-bold text-stone-900 dark:text-stone-100">
          The Anatomy of Common Indian Financial Scams
        </h2>

        <div class="space-y-4 text-xs sm:text-sm">
          <div class="p-5 rounded-xl border border-stone-200 dark:border-stone-800 bg-white dark:bg-stone-900 space-y-2">
            <h3 class="font-serif font-bold text-base text-stone-900 dark:text-stone-100 flex items-center justify-between">
              <span>1. The Multi-Level Marketing (MLM) & Ponzi Machine</span>
              <span class="text-xs font-mono text-red-600 font-normal">BUDS Act Violation</span>
            </h3>
            <p class="text-stone-600 dark:text-stone-400 leading-relaxed">
              <strong>The Mechanics:</strong> Early investors are paid "returns" directly out of the capital deposited by newer recruits rather than from genuine operational profits. Operators promise "1% daily" or "24% guaranteed annual return".
            </p>
            <p class="text-stone-600 dark:text-stone-400 leading-relaxed">
              <strong>Historical Case Studies:</strong> <em>Saradha Group</em> (₹2,500 Crore chit-fund fraud in West Bengal) and <em>PACL / Pearls</em> (₹49,100 Crore collective investment scheme disguised as agricultural land allocation).
            </p>
          </div>

          <div class="p-5 rounded-xl border border-stone-200 dark:border-stone-800 bg-white dark:bg-stone-900 space-y-2">
            <h3 class="font-serif font-bold text-base text-stone-900 dark:text-stone-100 flex items-center justify-between">
              <span>2. Stock Market Pump-and-Dump & Operator Syndicates</span>
              <span class="text-xs font-mono text-amber-600 font-normal">SEBI PFUTP Violation</span>
            </h3>
            <p class="text-stone-600 dark:text-stone-400 leading-relaxed">
              <strong>The Mechanics:</strong> Operators accumulate illiquid micro-cap or SME shares, orchestrate fake trade volume through circular trading accounts to trigger upper circuits, and pay financial influencers or Telegram channels to hype the stock. Once retail rushes in, the operator dumps the entire holding, leaving the stock locked in lower circuits with zero buyers.
            </p>
            <p class="text-stone-600 dark:text-stone-400 leading-relaxed">
              <strong>Historical Case Studies:</strong> The <em>Sadhna Broadcast</em> and <em>Sharpline Broadcast</em> YouTube manipulation orders issued by SEBI, where actors and finfluencers were banned and illegal profits impounded.
            </p>
          </div>

          <div class="p-5 rounded-xl border border-stone-200 dark:border-stone-800 bg-white dark:bg-stone-900 space-y-2">
            <h3 class="font-serif font-bold text-base text-stone-900 dark:text-stone-100 flex items-center justify-between">
              <span>3. Fake Trading Apps & "Pig-Butchering" Crypto Scams</span>
              <span class="text-xs font-mono text-red-600 font-normal">Cybercrime & PMLA</span>
            </h3>
            <p class="text-stone-600 dark:text-stone-400 leading-relaxed">
              <strong>The Mechanics:</strong> Victims are lured through WhatsApp or dating apps into joining "VIP institutional trading groups". They are instructed to download a proprietary APK or web app mimicking an institutional trading terminal showing huge fictitious profits. When the victim attempts to withdraw funds, they are told to deposit 20% "clearance tax" before all contact is severed.
            </p>
          </div>

          <div class="p-5 rounded-xl border border-stone-200 dark:border-stone-800 bg-white dark:bg-stone-900 space-y-2">
            <h3 class="font-serif font-bold text-base text-stone-900 dark:text-stone-100 flex items-center justify-between">
              <span>4. Institutional Liquidity Freezes & Credit Contagion</span>
              <span class="text-xs font-mono text-indigo-600 font-normal">Regulatory Lessons</span>
            </h3>
            <p class="text-stone-600 dark:text-stone-400 leading-relaxed">
              <strong>The Mechanics:</strong> Mutual funds or NBFCs take excessive duration or credit risk in unlisted, illiquid papers. When credit rating downgrades occur, secondary market buyers vanish, triggering massive redemption runs.
            </p>
            <p class="text-stone-600 dark:text-stone-400 leading-relaxed">
              <strong>Historical Case Studies:</strong> <em>Franklin Templeton’s 2020 wind-up</em> of 6 yield-oriented debt schemes (₹25,000 Crores frozen until secondary recoveries) and the <em>IL&FS & DHFL commercial paper collapses</em> (2018–2019).
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <!-- Whistleblower & Complaint Portals -->
      <section class="space-y-4">
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-serif font-bold text-stone-900 dark:text-stone-100">
          Official Investor Grievance & Complaint Channels
        </h2>
        <div class="grid grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-3 gap-4 text-xs">
          <div class="p-4 rounded-lg bg-stone-50 dark:bg-stone-800/60 border border-stone-200 dark:border-stone-700">
            <strong class="font-serif text-sm block mb-1">SEBI SCORES 2.0</strong>
            <p class="text-stone-500 mb-2">For complaints against listed companies, brokers, mutual funds, and depositories.</p>
            <a href="https://scores.sebi.gov.in" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="text-amber-600 hover:underline font-mono">scores.sebi.gov.in →</a>
          </div>

          <div class="p-4 rounded-lg bg-stone-50 dark:bg-stone-800/60 border border-stone-200 dark:border-stone-700">
            <strong class="font-serif text-sm block mb-1">RBI CMS & Sachet</strong>
            <p class="text-stone-500 mb-2">For banking grievances, NBFC P2P issues, and reporting unauthorized deposit-takers.</p>
            <a href="https://sachet.rbi.org.in" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="text-amber-600 hover:underline font-mono">sachet.rbi.org.in →</a>
          </div>

          <div class="p-4 rounded-lg bg-stone-50 dark:bg-stone-800/60 border border-stone-200 dark:border-stone-700">
            <strong class="font-serif text-sm block mb-1">National Cybercrime</strong>
            <p class="text-stone-500 mb-2">For fake trading apps, OTP theft, unauthorized UPI transfers, and crypto scams.</p>
            <a href="https://cybercrime.gov.in" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="text-amber-600 hover:underline font-mono">Call 1930 / cybercrime.gov.in →</a>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <Callout type="warning" title="The Golden Rule of Indian Investing">
        If anyone promises you <strong>guaranteed returns</strong> higher than the prevailing 10-year Sovereign Government of India bond yield (~7.0%), one of three things is guaranteed to be true: (1) They are taking catastrophic hidden credit risk; (2) They are operating an illegal Ponzi scheme under the BUDS Act 2019; or (3) You are the exit liquidity.
      </Callout>
    </div>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
